A||||2||Eric||Bumper Removal
Z||000000||Eric||07-24-99||09:05 AM||||How do you remove the plastic pins holdin the rear bumper in place.  There seems to be a notch in the top for a special kind of tool.  I don't want to damage the pins by pulling because they are holding onto metal.
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||07-24-99||09:38 AM||||Just grab them with pliers. I did and they worked fine to reinstall it. 
Z||000002||Cooter||07-24-99||09:09 PM||||The small pin in the middle pulls up to release the clip. Most of the time when you get the small pin about half way out the whole clip pops out. If not, just pull the pin out and stick a screwdriver under the clip and pop it out.
